<title>CANADA: Canada agency details flaxseed cargo quality.</title>
<headline>Canada agency details flaxseed cargo quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Monday detailed the quality of flaxseed exports. All figures in percent except iodine.</p>
<p>QUALITY	 SHIPPING    No1 CW    No1 CW High Waste Content</p>
<p>Tonnes	  Aug-Oct     24,459    39,205</p>
<p>Oil	     Aug-Oct     44.3	42.4</p>
<p>Protein	 Aug-Oct     21.7	22.2</p>
<p>Iodine Value		 199	 196</p>
<p>Moisture	Aug-Oct	7.5	 7.6</p>
<p>Dockage	 Aug-Oct	1.9	 6.6</p>
<p>Note: Iodine value is measured in milligrams per 100 grams of oil and is a measure of unsaturated fatty acids.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
